<%# Awaiting confirmation, New senders, Recently bounced. One shape at three
    registers: the section's own name is on the wrapper and the type scale
    hangs off it in CSS, so no template asks which section it is drawing.

    Every section reaches here, empty or not, and prints its own line when it
    has nothing — the reason is on Subscriptions. The rows choose their own
    partial: two of the three sections list newsletters and link, the third
    lists mail that never became one and cannot. %>
<section class="pen__section pen__section--<%= section.name %>">
  <h2 class="pen__heading"><%= section.heading %></h2>

  <% if section.any? %>
    <ol class="pen__list"><%= render section.rows %></ol>
  <% else %>
    <p class="pen__empty"><%= section.empty %></p>
  <% end %>
</section>
